# U.S. Stoneworks — Quote Chatbot Setup (No Twilio)

Auto-replies to "what's my quote" messages on SMS, WhatsApp, and Email
with the exact line-item breakdown, e.g.:

```
734 Rancho Cir
Fullerton

13 lineal feet Coping Demolition $130
Scupper Installation, scupper and repair one tile $350
13 lineal feet Coping with double bullnose, concrete gray color $1,170
177 lineal feet Concrete Repair, coping. Filling holes / sanding surface
to make smooth for the steps $1,947

Total: $3,597
(Quote valid until 9/28/2026)

Email or text us anytime with questions — or visit
https://us-stoneworks.github.io/us-stoneworks/#contact to reach us
directly.
```

**How pricing accuracy is guaranteed:** dollar amounts always come
straight from the spreadsheet. Claude (Anthropic API) only ever writes
one warm intro sentence and interprets loosely-worded messages — it
never generates a number.

**Quote matching needs zero AI.** Finding the right quote for an
incoming message (`findQuote_` in the script) is plain JavaScript —
matching a quote number, phone number, email, or address against the
spreadsheet. The Anthropic API is only called once per reply, to write
one friendly intro sentence, and that's controlled by a single toggle:

```js
const USE_AI_INTRO_SENTENCE = true; // set to false: zero Anthropic API calls, ever
```

Set it to `false` and the bot still finds the correct quote and sends
the full, accurate price breakdown — it just skips the friendly opening
line. You can prove this yourself: in the Apps Script editor, run
`testMatchingWithoutAI()` (function dropdown → select it → Run → View →
Logs) — it exercises quote matching end-to-end without touching Claude
at all.

## What changed from the Twilio version

| Channel | Was | Now |
|---|---|---|
| WhatsApp | Twilio (BSP, ~$0.005/msg markup on top of Meta's rate) | **Meta's WhatsApp Cloud API, direct** — no BSP, no markup |
| SMS | Twilio | **SMS Gateway for Android** — free, open source, self-hosted on a spare Android phone + SIM |
| Email | Gmail polling via Apps Script | Unchanged |
| AI | Anthropic API | Unchanged |

Trade-off, plainly: both alternatives save the per-message markup and
avoid a Twilio account, but you do more of the setup yourself, and the
SMS path depends on a physical phone staying online.

